    "summary": "Hardwood club (used for fish) carved with the head of a large sea monster, mammalian in form and with large raised nostrils, the eyes, teeth and mouth, and nostrils indicated with simple, possibly archaic style, formline designs. The club is slightly curved, with an indentation at the end for the handle, the latter with rows of crude incisions to provide grip, and a raised butt at the finial. It is extremely well worn and old, slightly cracked with some worming under the chin.",
